  "scoreProvenance": [
    "The complete concerto archive is immutable; winter-score-2.mid and the winter3 source definitions select only movement 3. Its published MIDI contains 2696 sounding note attacks over 229.5 quarter-note units.",
    "Source staves are solo violin, violin I, violin II, viola, and the written organ/cello bass line. Figured-bass symbols are retained visually but no realised continuo pitches or inferred separate double-bass part are invented. The source maintainer explicitly uses Anonymous.",
    "The Commons file history reports a lossless trim on 24 September 2011 without identifying its location. This alone is not evidence of a musical cut; full written-order correspondence must survive alignment and overlay inspection.",
    "Verified derivative syntax repair in winter-lys/winter3.ly: At source mark N, replace removed automatic-beam Scheme calls with their exact rhythmic intent: 32nd-note beams end at 1/8 and 2/8 in 3/8, hence groups 4+4+4. Retain the default whole-bar eighth-note exception. Only a disposable derivative changes, behind full published MIDI pitch/onset multiset proof.",
    "Verified derivative syntax repair in winter-lys/winter3a.ly: Preserve violin I’s source mark-N 32nd-note beaming boundaries at each eighth of the 3/8 bar using modern 4+4+4 beamExceptions; pitches, note order and durations are unchanged.",
    "Verified derivative syntax repair in winter-lys/winter3b.ly: Preserve violin II’s source mark-N 32nd-note beaming boundaries at each eighth of the 3/8 bar using modern 4+4+4 beamExceptions; pitches, note order and durations are unchanged.",
    "Verified derivative syntax repair in winter-lys/winter3c.ly: Preserve viola’s source mark-N 32nd-note beaming boundaries at each eighth of the 3/8 bar using modern 4+4+4 beamExceptions; pitches, note order and durations are unchanged.",
    "Verified derivative syntax repair in winter-lys/winter3d.ly: Preserve the written bass’s source mark-N 32nd-note beaming boundaries at each eighth of the 3/8 bar using modern 4+4+4 beamExceptions; pitches, note order and durations are unchanged."
  ],
